#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114979 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce2e21aa-f89d-5d10-b815-c66a2b46ef5c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product"}] :question/id #uuid "87bf279f-9f78-54cb-b9c3-e1bf1c5426ff" :question/math-academy-id "e-4505" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n${2x = 5; - 5x + 6y =-8$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation. The variable $y$ does not appear in the first equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0$. So, we get\n\n$$\n{2x + 0y = 5; - 5x + 6y =-8\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form\n\n$$\nA\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation\n\n$$\nA\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nbecomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114980 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4f746a1-ea9e-5136-90d6-d4dee1306c17" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product by Reorganizing"}] :question/id #uuid "359f4b72-60d2-54e2-b7ef-c48f1e3af708" :question/math-academy-id "e-4506" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n${-5y =-3x; 6 + x =-2 + y$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order:\n\n$$\n{3x - 5y = 0; x - y =-8\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form\n\n$$\nA\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation\n\n$$\nA\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nbecomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114981 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2300a1-f31e-5a24-889a-6f45e1e8647b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Matrix Product as a 2x2 System of Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "b87aa5eb-f689-5f34-baeb-f97c3f200552" :question/math-academy-id "e-4507" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n$\\begin{bmatrix}10 & -15 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "The $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y$, while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{10x - 15y = 5; 1x + 0y =-2\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n{2x - 3y = 1; x =-2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115652 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2300a1-f31e-5a24-889a-6f45e1e8647b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Matrix Product as a 2x2 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ddf0cd7f-e5e4-5843-9832-6ff022f43e14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2x - 5y = 10; x =-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113313} {:answer/id #uuid "02f87275-1680-5e69-b30f-e34823497555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2x + 5y =-7; x = 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113314} {:answer/id #uuid "36ec4f5e-d9de-58bf-88e1-fb9f8dc1838e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2x - 5y =-7; x = 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113315} {:answer/id #uuid "4c68845b-874c-5896-9f16-ac96d40fe1b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2x + 5y = 10; y =-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113316} {:answer/id #uuid "4f327003-eb35-5ffb-a303-754812dc5872" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2x - 5y = 10; y =-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddf0cd7f-e5e4-5843-9832-6ff022f43e14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2x - 5y = 10; x =-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113313} :answer-field/id #uuid "83377318-ace5-5f3b-836e-6b1faff567b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113312}] :question/id #uuid "d80073fa-9f5d-593f-a765-d5bf9c3d142b" :question/math-academy-id "q-31876" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}$?"}]}
